    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** headlining the offensive unit, boasting a standout score of 75.27. His matchup against Merrill Kelly (xERA 5.37) is the most favorable on the board, compounded by a strong platoon advantage and a projected spot in the #2 hole, which maximizes his exposure to run-scoring opportunities. Joining him in the top tier are **Gunnar Henderson** (68.29) and **Jacob Wilson** (66.45). While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight negative platoon adjustment against the southpaw Peterson, his raw talent and placement in the heart of the order keep his floor high. **Jacob Wilson** remains a sharp play, as his efficiency rating is buoyed by favorable park factors and an assumed #5 spot that should provide ample RBI potential against Framber Valdez.\n\nWe have opted to bench **Miguel Vargas** despite his solid 42.64 efficiency score, as he fell just outside the optimal rotation against Patrick Sandoval. While his elite xwOBA of .403 is tempting, the combination of a tough park and the lack of a favorable platoon edge made him the odd man out in favor of players like **Dominic Smith** and **Nolan Schanuel**, who offer more predictable pathing to counting stats today. **Heliot Ramos** serves as a high-upside pivot, with his 65.18 score bolstered by a helpful wind forecast that could turn a routine fly ball into a scoring event, reinforcing our strategy of chasing high-ceiling park environments.\n\nCaution is advised regarding the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Jacob Wilson**, **Josh Jung**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Josh Lowe**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Nolan Schanuel**. Any late-breaking changes to their batting order will fluctuate their projected efficiency scores significantly. Additionally, **Josh Lowe** faces a difficult task against Nathan Eovaldi (xERA 3.38); while his platoon edge is significant, the threat of Eovaldi\u2019s command keeps his score at a marginal 46.03. We are closely monitoring the weather and lineup cards to ensure no late-hour shifts mandate a swap for bench depth like **Sam Antonacci** or **Denzer Guzman**, though currently, our optimized starters provide the best probability of maintaining our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories.",
